eversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that a failure to clear push_state during reconciliation is swallowed and the probe still returns `fresh` (preserving the 'never block a healthy gate' contract), and note whether the clear is idempotent/safe under a concurrent push writer.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.851,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Reconciling means clearing the persisted push_state so the next probe is cheap, not merely ignoring it at read time'","Plan (Why worth fixing): the probe 'deliberately degrades to fresh on any internal failure' and 'a broken diagnostic must never be able to block a healthy gate'","ABSENCE: no statement of what store_freshness returns if the push_state clear raises an I/O error or races a concurrent push writer"],"finding":"The approach converts a read-only, fail-safe probe into one that performs a persisted WRITE (clearing push_state on a level store), but does not specify the failure behavior of that write.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff3310a3ceac9040c","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section: 'Reconciling means clearing the persisted `push_state`'","norm_id":"n8701ba3cc5d7254f","priority":0.099,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The clear write fails (disk full, permission, concurrent write) after refs are determined level — does the probe still return fresh, or does the exception propagate and re-wedge the gate the fix was meant to unblock?"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to the Approach: on a level store, attempt to clear push_state, but if the clear raises, still return verdict `fresh` (consistent with the degrade-to-fresh contract); make the clear tolerant of a concurrent writer / already-cleared state.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"State the ownership and atomicity of the push_state clear performed during reconciliation — confirm the probe's write cannot race a concurrent rebar push writer (e.g. it clears only when refs are observably level AND the recorded pending predates the current level state), or document why the probe is the sole writer at that moment.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.785,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["'Reconciling means clearing the persisted push_state so the next probe is cheap, not merely ignoring it at read time'","push_state is a persisted shared record read by the freshness probe and written by the push path; the plan introduces a second writer (the probe) without stating how the two writers coordinate.","T9 checklist: 'Update concurrency / ownership is clear' and 'mutated atomically ... no check-then-act TOCTOU'."],"finding":"The plan adds a RETIRE/clear path for the persisted push_state sentinel (reconcile on a level store) but does not state the ownership or concurrency discipline of that write — whether clearing the sentinel can race a concurrent rebar-performed push that is legitimately setting/holding pending, and whether the clear is atomic against that writer.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff1b45bf550619917","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Reconciling means clearing the persisted push_state so the next probe is cheap'","norm_id":"nf5564cdf280ac9ba","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A rebar-performed push is in flight (has set pending) while HEAD momentarily reads level against a stale origin/tickets ref, and the probe clears the sentinel that the push writer still owns.","Two probes / a probe and a push concurrently read-then-write push_state, one clobbering the other's state."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","